  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of labour migration and mobility in line with ILS in Suriname</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports Suriname in strengthening labour migration governance to better protect migrant workers and promote fair, well-managed labour mobility. Aligned with Suriname&#x2019;s Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) 2023&#x2013;2026 and ILO Programme and Budget Outcome 6: Protection at work for all, the initiative addresses key challenges related to irregular migration, weak oversight of recruitment practices, and gaps in labour migration data. The ILO will provide technical assistance, training, and capacity building to government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organisations to strengthen fair recruitment practices, improve coordination through tripartite dialogue, and enhance the national evidence base on labour migration. This includes supporting the development of a national labour migration policy framework, adapting practical fair recruitment tools, and improving data collection and analysis on migrant workers. The project aims to reduce risks of labour exploitation, support evidence-based policy making, and ensure that labour migration contributes to decent work, labour market needs, and inclusive development in Suriname.</narrative>
  </description>
